<div style="border: 2px solid #1a5276; padding: 15px; text-align: center; background-color: #eaf2f8;">
    <h1 style="color: #1a5276; margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # 1 – Lesson # 1</h1>
    <p style="color: #1a5276; margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-style: italic;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 1</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Listening</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 6th Grade (CEFR: A2.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Keeping Our Communities Clean</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> Who Will Bring the Cleaning Supplies?</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Interpret audio clips from class lessons to support class discussions.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can identify specific details in spoken announcements about the school (e.g., 'The school will launch a cleaning campaign tomorrow.'). Can interpret key details from audio clips about the community (e.g., 'We need to clean the river.'). Can discuss main points about keeping communities clean (e.g., 'We should work together.').</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 30%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 20%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays pictures of a dirty park and a clean park. Students observe the pictures. The teacher asks, "What do you see?" and guides students to say "dirty park" and "clean park." The teacher then asks, "Which park do you like?" and "What can we do to make a dirty park clean?" to introduce the theme.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher introduces key vocabulary words related to community cleaning using flashcards and gestures: 'community', 'trash', 'supplies', 'clean' (verb), 'bring', 'pick up', 'work', 'recycling'. The teacher models the pronunciation, paying special attention to the word stress on imperative commands like 'Bring a bag!' and 'Clean the park!' The teacher also models the short /ɪ/ sound in 'bring' and the long /iː/ sound in 'clean', differentiating them clearly for students.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of new vocabulary.
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(For 'trash'): "Is trash good for the park?" (Expected answer: "No.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">(For 'supplies'): "Are brooms and bags cleaning supplies?" (Expected answer: "Yes.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher asks students to repeat the new words chorally and individually, focusing on clear pronunciation.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5-7 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Keeping Our Communities Clean".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> Short audio announcements (e.g., from a school principal or a community leader) about an upcoming cleaning campaign. The audio clips will include target grammar (modal verbs like 'should', 'can', 'must', future tense 'will', and imperatives) and vocabulary (community, supplies, trash, pick up, recycle, clean, work, bring).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening: Can identify specific details in spoken announcements about the school and community.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher tells students they will listen to two short audio clips about cleaning up.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>First Listen (Gist):</b> Students listen to Audio 1. The teacher asks a gist question: "What is the announcement about? (A) A school party. (B) A cleaning day. (C) A new park." (Expected answer: B)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Second Listen (Specific Details):</b> Students listen to Audio 1 again. The teacher provides a simple True/False activity or matching task. For example:
                        <br><i>Audio 1: "Attention, students! The school will launch a cleaning campaign tomorrow, Friday, at 9 AM. We should clean the classrooms. Volunteers must bring their own bags for trash."</i>
                        <ul>
                            <li>The cleaning campaign is tomorrow. (True/False)</li>
                            <li>Students should clean the park. (True/False)</li>
                            <li>Volunteers must bring cleaning supplies. (True/False)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Third Listen (Identifying key words):</b> Students listen to Audio 2. The teacher provides a list of 4-5 key vocabulary words from the audio (e.g., 'community', 'river', 'recycling', 'help'). Students tick the words they hear.
                        <br><i>Audio 2: "Hello, neighbors! Our community needs help. We will clean the river on Saturday. We can pick up trash and recycle plastic. Please come and work together!"</i>
                    </li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(10-12 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Listening.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice listening for specific vocabulary and grammatical structures (modal verbs: should, can, must; future tense: will; imperatives) related to describing plans and making suggestions for community cleaning.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Controlled Practice (Listen and Match):</b> The teacher plays parts of Audio 1 and 2 again. Students have a worksheet with two columns: "Who/What" and "Action/Detail". They listen and draw lines to match the information.
                        <br><i>Example:</i>
                        <ul>
                            <li>School cleaning campaign _____ tomorrow</li>
                            <li>Volunteers _____ bring bags</li>
                            <li>Community _____ needs help</li>
                            <li>We _____ clean the river</li>
                        </ul>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Semi-controlled Practice (Listen and Fill-in-the-Blank):</b> The teacher plays new, short sentences or slightly modified versions of the audio clips with gaps. Students listen and fill in the missing target vocabulary (e.g., 'supplies', 'trash', 'recycling') or modal verbs ('should', 'will'). A word bank can be provided for support.
                        <br><i>Example Audio: "We ____ clean the park. Please ____ your own ____."</i>
                        <br><i>Worksheet: "We ______ clean the park. Please ______ your own ______." (Word bank: bring, should, bags)</i>
                    </li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Pair Interaction / Peer Check (Listen and Compare):</b> In pairs, students compare their answers from the fill-in-the-blank activity. The teacher plays the audio snippets one last time for self-correction. Students orally check their partner's answers, practicing phrases like "I heard 'should'. What did you hear?"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(12-15 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Keeping Our Communities Clean".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format: Listening for Instructions and Reporting</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The teacher divides the class into small groups (3-4 students). Each group will listen to a short audio message from a "community leader" giving instructions for different tasks for a cleanup day, including who should bring what supplies. The audio will specifically address the theme "Who Will Bring the Cleaning Supplies?" and the scenario "Keeping Our Communities Clean".</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group receives a simple chart with columns: "Task", "Who", "What to Bring".</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher plays a new audio clip (e.g., "Hello team! For the park cleanup, Group 1 will pick up trash. You should bring big bags. Group 2 will collect recycling. You can bring plastic bins. Group 3 will clean the swings. You must bring sponges and water. We will start at 8 AM on Saturday.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students listen carefully and collaboratively fill in their group's chart with the details they hear. They may listen two or three times.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">After listening, each group briefly reports back one detail from their chart to the class (e.g., "Group 1 will pick up trash. They should bring big bags."). This encourages collaborative listening and simple verbal reporting using target vocabulary and grammar.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(8-10 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students complete a short listening comprehension quiz based on a final audio announcement. The quiz will have 3-4 multiple-choice or short-answer questions. For example, "When will the cleanup be?" "What should volunteers bring?" "What will they clean?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Accuracy in identifying specific details from the audio (e.g., correct time, location, items).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'supplies', 'trash', 'recycling') when answering if applicable.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of answers.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students answer on a small slip of paper:
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. One new word I learned today is ______.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. I can understand (some / most / all) of the cleaning announcements.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(5-7 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was easy for me when listening today?</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What was difficult for me when listening today?</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this listening lesson? (e.g., The multiple listens, the visual aids, the pair work).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for the next lesson (Lesson 2)? (e.g., More visual support for new vocabulary, slower audio pace, or pre-teaching specific phrases). The pronunciation focus on /ɪ/ and /iː/ sounds might need more specific drill next time.</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In Lesson 2, students will encounter the same core vocabulary and grammatical structures in a written text, focusing on reading comprehension about community cleaning initiatives, reinforcing the understanding established through listening today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(3 min)</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>